 "Chronic Hematological Malignancy: Blasts and constitutional symptoms suggest a subacute rather than insidious progression", "Systemic Inflammatory Syndrome: Constitutional symptoms could overlap, but blasts are more specific for malignancy"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (malaise, night sweats, weight loss)", "Pancytopenia with blasts (high-grade suspicion for leukemia)", "Visual acuity decline and ataxia (possible paraneoplastic or metastatic involvement)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.6469413686694501, "posterior": 0.3929677930686649, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The combination of blasts, pancytopenia, and subacute progression provides moderate support for myeloid neoplasm (AML/MDS) over other categories."], "evidence_against": ["Subacute clinical progression moderately supports chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm in blast crisis (CML) over de novo myeloid/lymphoid neoplasms."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.124, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of lymphadenopathy and non-lymphoblastic morphology weakly disfavors ALL as the primary diagnosis."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.06, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": [